        "title": "Digital Comics and Webcomics",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n+------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                  DIGITAL AND WEBCOMICS LANDSCAPE                 |\n|                                                                  |\n|  FORMATS                                                         |\n|  Webcomic: published directly to web; free; creator-to-reader    |\n|  Digital comics: scanned/digital versions of print comics        |\n|  Webtoon: vertical-scroll format; Korean manhwa origin           |\n|  Motion comics: animated comics panels                           |\n|  Digital-first: publisher digital releases before print          |\n|                                                                  |\n|  MARKET (2024)                                                   |\n|  comiXology/Amazon: dominant digital comics storefront (US)      |\n|  Naver Webtoon: largest webtoon platform; 100M+ monthly users    |\n|  Tapas: US webtoon platform                                      |\n|  Manga Plus: Shueisha's free manga platform                      |\n|                                                                  |\n|  ECONOMICS SHIFT                                                 |\n|  Old: publisher -> distribution -> comic shop -> reader          |\n|  New: creator -> platform -> reader (or creator direct)          |\n+------------------------------------------------------------------+\n```"
